/* GPIO_RETAIN: RETAIN of each individual GPIO pin. Pins with their RETAIN bit set keep their state independent of changes of
                 the GPIO-configuration and peripheral changes. RETAIN must be cleared before the pin can be used. RETAIN is
                 typically used to isolate the pin state from internal device state changes. The pin will keep all its state
                 including the output value, DIR and PORTCNF settings. */

  #define GPIO_RETAIN_ResetValue (0xFFFFFFFFUL)      /*!< Reset value of RETAIN register.                                      */

